Here's how to handle each scenario with modern MSTest (3.9+/3.10+):

## 1. Windows-only tests — `[OSCondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    var value = Registry.GetValue(@"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\...", "Key", null);
    Assert.IsNotNull(value);
}
```

The test is automatically skipped (not failed) on Linux/macOS.

## 2. Skip in CI — `[CICondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
public void GpuRendering_ProducesExpectedOutput()
{
    // Only runs locally, skipped in CI
    var result = GpuRenderer.Render(scene);
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

## 3. Flaky external API — `[Retry]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)]
[Timeout(10000)]
public async Task WeatherApi_ReturnsForecast(TestContext testContext)
{
    var forecast = await _weatherClient.GetForecastAsync(testContext.CancellationToken);
    Assert.IsNotNull(forecast);
}
```

The test retries up to 3 times before reporting failure. Use `[Timeout]` with `CancellationToken` so hung calls don't block indefinitely.

## 4. Cleanup temp files even on failure — `[TestCleanup]`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public sealed class FileProcessorTests
{
    private string _tempFile = string.Empty;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void Process_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        FileProcessor.Process(_tempFile);
        var content = File.ReadAllText(_tempFile);
        Assert.Contains("expected", content);
    }

    [TestCleanup]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs even if the test throws
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }
}
```

`[TestCleanup]` always runs after each test method regardless of pass/fail/exception.

---

**Key points:**
- `[OSCondition]` requires MSTest 3.10+
- `[CICondition]` requires MSTest 3.10+
- `[Retry]` requires MSTest 3.9+
- `[TestCleanup]` has always been available and is guaranteed to execute after each test
